  "figure": {
    "caption": "Separation by the Markov chain of [Cannon2019Separation]: one particle at a time (outlined) expands into a free neighbouring node and contracts forward with probability $\\lambda^{\\Delta e}\\gamma^{\\Delta h}$ ($\\Delta e$, $\\Delta h$: the change in its neighbours and in its neighbours of its own colour; certainly if the product is at least 1), and otherwise contracts back; moves that would disconnect the system or create a hole are refused. The chain also lets neighbours of different colours swap places (not shown). For large $\\lambda$ and $\\gamma$ the system becomes compressed and separated with high probability; for $\\gamma$ close to 1 it stays integrated.",
